=== root cause ===
store.py uses ONE transaction per investigation. _save_pattern hits the
investigation_memory schema fork (column 'task_type' does not exist), which
aborts the postgres transaction. The Python try/except catches the python
exception but the underlying postgres txn is poisoned — every subsequent
statement is rejected, and conn.commit() implicitly rolls everything back.
The _update_task_status UPDATE that ran successfully (with model_name='unknown')
is rolled back along with everything else. Task stays pending.
